          "title": "You'll want to know: булочная",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "булочная (búlochnaya) — \"a bakery (shop)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Утром я покупаю хлеб в булочной. Útrom ya pokupáyu khleb v búlochnoy. In the morning I buy bread at the bakery."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "An adjective used as a noun. Traditionally чн is pronounced шн here."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "булочная (búlochnaya) is built on булочка, булка 'a roll' with an adjective ending: the shop for rolls. EtymDB lists булка without a deeper source."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
