              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "гастроном (gastronóm) — \"a grocery store, a food shop\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "В гастрономе на углу мы купили сыр и колбасу. V gastronóme na uglú my kupíli syr i kolbasú. We bought cheese and sausage at the grocery store on the corner."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine. Also an old word for a gourmet."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "гастроном (gastronóm) is usually traced, probably through French gastronome, to Greek gastḗr 'belly' and nómos 'law': first a gourmet, then a food shop. EtymDB does not list it, so the line is hedged."
            }
          ]
        },
